?sensor -hydrorwth:monitorsCatchment-> envthes:30212;  
?sosa_obs -sosa:hasFeatureOfInterest-> envthes:30212;  
?sosa_obs -sosa:observedProperty-> envthes:21524;  
?sosa_obs -sosa:resultTime-> ?time

Interpretation:  
The path identifies temperature observations made by the sensor named “brora at bruachrobie,” links them to the monitored catchment via the sensor/catchment rule, restricts the observed property to Temperature (envthes:21524), and uses the observation result plus result time to evaluate frost days as temperatures below 0°C between 2000 and 2010.
